## Why This Matters
This interview question tests your understanding of macro correctness, multi-tenant schema templating, and CI/CD integration for data quality enforcement.

## Key Concepts
- dbt macros and singular/generic tests
- Per-tenant schemas using `analytics_{{tenant}}` naming convention
- CI gating: blocking deploys when any tenant's test reports NULL violations

## Code Example
```sql
-- analytics_base/macros/not_null_guard.sql
{% macro not_null_guard(tenant, model, col) %}
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM analytics_{{ tenant }}.{{ model }} WHERE {{ col }} IS NULL) = 0
{% endmacro %}
```

```sql
-- tests/generic/not_null_guard.sql
{% test not_null_guard(model, col) %}
  {% if execute %}
    {% set result = run_query(not_null_guard(this.name, model, col)) %}
    {% if result.rows[0][0] | int != 0 %}
      {% do exceptions.raise_compile_error(
        "Failed: " ~ model ~ "." ~ col ~ " contains NULL values"
      ) %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
{% endtest %}
```

The test verifies zero NULL values exist in the target column across all tenant-specific models.

## Why This Is Asked
Tests handling of per-tenant incremental pipelines, simple data freshness logic, and a CI gate without deep complexity.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant incremental models
- Data freshness checks and basic SLA gates
- dbt tests: not_null and unique; backfill strategy
- Lightweight CI integration for production guardrails

## Code Example
```javascript
// sketch of a freshness macro concept (dbt uses SQL/Jinja; shown here for clarity)
function freshness_check(tenant_id, event_date) {
  const maxDate = `SELECT tenant_id, MAX(${event_date}) as max_date FROM {{ this }} GROUP BY tenant_id`;
  // compare to current_date and decide SLA breach
  return `CASE WHEN DATEDIFF(current_date, max_date) > 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END`;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to handle partial backfills for previously SLA-compliant tenants?
- What metrics or dashboards would you add to monitor SLA adherence over time?
